}

\p{These are the 351 of [the decision that introduced the net](dec-7UAL). Without the net every one of the 485 files is rejected, which is the official verdict of each. All 351 are mutants of the kind that wraps one expression in a metadata record (\code{\verb~|wrap_mdata~}) and whose source test the official checker rejects: 67 in the tutorial corpus, 37 in the bugs corpus, 247 in the metadata corpus, from 104 source tests. The patch comes with the list of every mutant whose verdict moves, by name.}
}

\subtree{
\title{5. The machine alone against the official verdicts}

\subtree{
\title{5.1 Every input set under the three configurations}

\p{"Agree" is the official verdict. "Tolerated" is an accept of a row or test whose statement is derivable and which the official checker rejects, the kind T of [the exactness contract](design-exactness-contract-kinds). No file of any set is an accept of a statement that is not derivable, kind F, in any configuration: turning the re-check, the net or the fallback off can only turn an accept into a rejection or a decline, and the files show nothing else.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Input set}\th{Configuration}\th{Agree}\th{Tolerated accept}\th{Wrong reject}\th{Declined}\th{Wrong accept}}
\tr{\td{eight corpora}\td{old default}\td{8}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{}\td{new default}\td{8}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{}\td{machine alone}\td{2}\td{0}\td{0}\td{6}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{arena, 262 small tests: 140 good, 92 bad, 30 \code{either}}\td{all three}\td{258: 140 accepted, 92 rejected, and 26 of the \code{either} tests}\td{2 of the \code{either} tests}\td{0}\td{2 of the \code{either} tests, on which the official kernel does not terminate}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{mutants, 17,775}\td{old default}\td{15,741}\td{0}\td{0}\td{2,034}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{}\td{new default}\td{16,092}\td{0}\td{0}\td{1,683}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{}\td{machine alone}\td{16,090}\td{0}\td{0}\td{1,685}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{hostile suite, 1,274}\td{old default}\td{1,192}\td{78}\td{0}\td{4}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{}\td{new default}\td{1,184}\td{74}\td{\strong{12}}\td{4}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{}\td{machine alone}\td{1,180}\td{74}\td{\strong{12}}\td{8}\td{0}}
}

\p{The two tolerated accepts of the arena are \code{\verb~|corner-cases/alg-conv-trans-quot-left~} and \code{\verb~|corner-cases/eta-struct-major-and~}: the default set accepts them, the machine without the two shortcuts, the machine without any switch and the reference engine reject them as the official checker does. The arena allows either verdict there. By corpus the mutants of the new default are 11,847 and 413 (tutorial), 2,627 and 65 (bugs), 779 and 1,197 (metadata), 839 and 8 (prelude).}
}

\subtree{
\title{5.2 The twelve known wrong rejects}

\p{All twelve are official accepts that the machine's primary lane rejects; all twelve carried the note \code{recheck} in the manifest of the hostile suite, which said that the pipeline repairs them. Two causes.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Cause}\th{Rows}\th{What makes the machine reject}\th{Who accepts}}
\tr{\td{A memo that survives a declaration (the switch \code{warm}; [class 3](design-official-divergence-memo), finding S3-F3)}\td{8: \code{\verb~|s3-wc-proj-two-decls-ok~}, \code{\verb~|s3-wc-warm-samehead-two-decls-ok~}, \code{\verb~|r2-ptr-alone-ok~}, \code{\verb~|r2-ptr-other-record-order-ok~}, \code{\verb~|r2-ptr-same-record-ok~}, \code{\verb~|r2-ptr-same-record-def-ok~}, \code{\verb~|oh-kept-false-reused-ok~}, \code{\verb~|oh-kept-false-then-true-ok~}}\td{An earlier declaration of the file left the full reduction of a projection, or a negative comparison result, in the session; a later declaration asks the cheap question and gets the full answer. Officially every cache lives for one declaration.}\td{The machine itself in a fresh session: with \code{\verb~|default,-warm~}, with the session forgotten before every declaration, and as the strict machine of the re-check.}}
\tr{\td{Tables keyed by values, with canonical variables ([class 2](design-official-divergence-pairs), finding S3-F1)}\td{4: \code{\verb~|s3-wc-canon-fvar-full-first-ok~}, \code{\verb~|r2-id-binder-name-ok~}, \code{\verb~|r2-id-binder-name-def-ok~}, \code{\verb~|r2-id-binder-info-ok~}}\td{Inside one declaration. Officially the second lambda has a new variable and an empty cache for its terms, or the accept is an answer of the cache of successful pairs for two terms that differ in a binder name or a binder info only; the machine's memo of the full reduction is keyed by the value under one canonical variable.}\td{The reference engine only; the machine rejects with every switch set, the one without switches included.}}
}

\p{What aligning would take is written down in [the review of the default set](rep-soundness-default-set), section 5, cheapest first: a two-answer rule that decides a comparison for the stuck projection and for its full reduction and declines when the verdicts differ; no use of a comparison result, a checked type or a full reduction across declarations; or the official caches themselves, keyed by terms, per declaration, with a fresh variable per binder instance. The second closes the 8 rows of the first cause and is what the next section prices; only the third closes the 4 of the second cause without a decline, and its cost was never measured.}
}

\subtree{
\title{5.3 The tolerated accepts, by what produces them}

\p{The 74 tolerated accepts of the new default, each attributed by removing switches until the machine alone no longer accepts the row. The last column is what the journal has measured for the mechanism; none of it was measured again here. The times of the shortcuts and of \code{eager} are those of [the decision on the default set](dec-YP0N): warm wall clock of a pass that reloads the file, 8 workers, JVM launcher, aarch64 development host, the sets interleaved in quiet windows on 2026-11-24, before the two waves of 2026-11-25; "geometric mean" is over the eight corpora.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Mechanism}\th{Rows}\th{Which}\th{Aligning means}\th{What the mechanism is worth, as measured}}
\tr{\td{The shortcut \code{congruence}, outside eager reduction}\td{16}\td{the nine \code{probe-b1} and \code{probe-b12} rows, \code{\verb~|open-flag-closed-bad~}, \code{\verb~|s3-k2-krule-subst-bad~} and \code{\verb~|-hot-bad~}, \code{\verb~|s3-same-closure-proof-slot-bad~}, \code{\verb~|s2-acc-rec-intro-vs-axiom~}, the two \code{c1-fuse} rows}\td{The official argument comparison instead of the same-head probe, closure congruence and proofs by type, see [the shortcuts](design-proof-comparison-shortcuts).}\td{With \code{skipargs} already on: the geometric mean of the eight warm passes is 1.720 s with it and 1.801 s without, 4.7 \% longer; navier-stokes-euler 3.22 against 4.04 s, Mathlib 12.72 against 13.39 s.}}
\tr{\td{\code{congruence} under eager reduction}\td{22}\td{the family of the eager rows: 13 that the machine rejects without the shortcut, 9 that it declines without it (the rows with the note \code{eager-hard})}\td{The same, inside a declaration that enters eager reduction. Without the switch \code{eager} the machine declines all 22 and the reference engine gives the official rejection.}\td{As the row above. \code{eager} itself: 1.980 s against 2.065 s for the set of the wave-6 integration, Mathlib 18.02 against 20.49 s.}}
\tr{\td{The shortcut \code{skipargs}}\td{4}\td{the three \code{\verb~|e1-lam-fvar-type-in-conv~} rows, \code{\verb~|e1-sib-proj-let-pi-bad~}}\td{Compare proof positions and the positions a definition does not read.}\td{With \code{congruence} already on: 1.720 s with it, 1.758 s without, 2.2 \% longer; navier-stokes-euler 3.22 against 3.79 s.}}
\tr{\td{Either shortcut}\td{3}\td{the three accepted \code{facts} rows}\td{Both off.}\td{Both shortcuts together: 1.720 s against 1.980 s, the set without them is 15.1 \% longer; Mathlib 12.72 against 18.02 s, navier-stokes-euler 3.22 against 6.08 s, cslib 4.56 against 5.27 s.}}
\tr{\td{A memo that survives a declaration: \code{warm}}\td{11}\td{\code{\verb~|s3-wc-warm-pair-reused-bad~}, \code{\verb~|s3-wc-warm-term-reused-bad~} and \code{\verb~|-reset-bad~}, the four \code{oh-kept-true} rows, the four \code{oh-shape} rows}\td{No comparison result, checked type or full reduction kept across declarations. This is the same change that closes 8 of the wrong rejects of section 5.2.}\td{One worker, native image, the switches \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}, median CPU time of three rounds, warm sessions at the better of the caps of 2 and 4 MiB against no warm session: Init 7.71 against 8.13 s, Std 13.80 against 13.72 s, the Cedar slice 3.32 against 3.40 s, see [the session cap](dec-KXE1). Not measured with the present default set, and not for a session that keeps only values.}}
\tr{\td{\code{pchk} or \code{warm}: the shared check facts}\td{4}\td{the four \code{s3-pchk} rows}\td{Neither; each alone still accepts the rows.}\td{\code{pchk}: 1.5 to 1.8 \% fewer instructions on Init and Std alone, 3.7 and 4.3 \% with \code{match} and \code{joint}, see [the switch reference](design-switches-document). Instructions, not time.}}
\tr{\td{The tabling gate \code{gated}}\td{1}\td{\code{\verb~|e1-sib-krule-major-redex-bad~}}\td{The raw major premise of the K rule typed as a term, finding E1-F7.}\td{No time of its own in the journal: without it every node is tabled, and a nest of 4,000 unshared levels costs 8,038,031 ticks instead of 60,017.}}
\tr{\td{No switch: the machine on values}\td{9}\td{\code{\verb~|e1-sib-proj-applied-let-pi-bad~}, \code{\verb~|e1-sib-proj-redex-pi-bad~} (stand-in types, [class 1](design-official-divergence-standin)); \code{\verb~|s3-wc-canon-fvar-bad~}, \code{\verb~|s3-wc-pos-beta-bad~}, \code{\verb~|s3-wc-inner-rec-minor-bad~} (the pair table, class 2); \code{\verb~|r2-id-beta-control-bad~}, \code{\verb~|r2-id-literal-vs-offset-bad~}, \code{\verb~|r2-mdata-beta-plainform-bad~}, \code{\verb~|r2-mdata-beta-arg-plainform-bad~}}\td{The official type of an unreduced term, and the official caches keyed by terms.}\td{Not a switch, so nothing to turn off; the cost of an exact treatment was never measured.}}
\tr{\td{No switch: both engines}\td{4}\td{\code{\verb~|s3-wc-pos-mdata-bad~} (a dropped metadata node), \code{\verb~|r2-id-let-nondep-bad~} and \code{\verb~|-def-bad~} (the flag of a let), \code{\verb~|r2-adm-param-success-bad~} (the caches of admission)}\td{The loader and admission, not the machine: the reference engine accepts them under the practical policy too, see [class 5](design-official-divergence-reference).}\td{Nothing in time.}}
}

\ul{
\li{\strong{The four that only the re-check made.} \code{\verb~|s3-wc-inner-caseson-bad~} and \code{\verb~|s3-wc-inner-matcher-bad~} are rejected by the default set (through \code{casetrees}) and accepted by the machine without switches; \code{\verb~|r2-ptr-other-record-bad~} and \code{\verb~|-def-bad~} are rejected by a warm session and accepted by a fresh one. The old default accepted the four because the strict machine of the re-check accepted them. They are the reason why the suite has 78 tolerated accepts today and 74 without the re-check.}
\li{\strong{Outside the suite.} The two \code{either} tests of the arena of section 5.1 need the two shortcuts. The one hostile file with a repeated theorem, see [the accept of a repeat](design-verdict-protocol-repeats), is accepted through the repeat skip, which is worth 1.4 \% of the geometric mean in the executable (1.855 to 1.829 s) and 0.7 \% on the JVM launcher.}
\li{\strong{Read as a work list.} 45 of the 74 rows, and both arena tests, are the two proof-comparison shortcuts, which are also by far the largest single gain of the default set; 15 rows and 8 of the 12 wrong rejects are the memos of a warm session, which gain little where they were measured; 13 rows and 4 wrong rejects need the official caches and types, for which no design exists.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{5.4 The schedule}

\p{[The driver](design-driver-invariants) states that the verdict does not depend on the worker count, the session cap or the load mode. Its invariance suite, \src{rlvm-driver/bin/invariance.sh}, runs every file under nine schedules: batch with 1, 2, 4 and 8 forced workers, a session cap of one byte with 1 and 4 workers, and pipelined loading with a publication after every 1, 7 and 64 units. Run here with the machine as primary engine, in the patched private tree:}

\table{
\tr{\th{Input}\th{Protocol}\th{Files}\th{Files with a schedule difference}\th{Which}}
\tr{\td{hostile suite}\td{re-check on, the old default}\td{1,274}\td{12}\td{the 11 tolerated accepts that need \code{warm}: accepted with the history of a session, rejected when every declaration has a fresh one. And \code{\verb~|oh-kept-false-then-false-bad~}, rejected in eight schedules and accepted with 4 workers and a publication every 7 units.}}
\tr{\td{hostile suite}\td{re-check off, the new default}\td{1,274}\td{21}\td{the same 11; the 8 wrong rejects of the first cause of section 5.2 and the two \code{\verb~|r2-ptr-other-record~} rows, all rejected with the history and accepted without. \code{\verb~|r2-ptr-same-record-def-ok~} is also accepted with 8 workers, where its two declarations go to two sessions.}}
\tr{\td{the 231 published tests of the suite's list}\td{re-check off}\td{231}\td{0}\td{}}
\tr{\td{mutants, tutorial}\td{re-check off}\td{12,260}\td{0}\td{}}
\tr{\td{mutants, bugs and metadata}\td{re-check off}\td{4,668}\td{0}\td{}}
}

\p{So the invariant never held for the machine on hostile input: an accept that rests on a warm memo already depends on the schedule today. Without the re-check the same is true of the rejections that rest on one, which nearly doubles the rows, and one of them moves with the worker count alone. On the published tests and the mutants no verdict moves. The re-check hid the second half of this because a fresh strict machine repairs exactly the rejections a history produces. The property that would restore the invariant in both directions is the one priced in section 5.3: no answer of a comparison, a checked type or a full reduction kept from one declaration to the next. Recorded as [an insight](ins-RPOG).}
}
}

